																		Here&#039;s my linebyline of the description
															</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/henzoid" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(5190300); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=5190300&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1607200985" alt="Henzoid" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=5190300)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/henzoid" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(5190300); return false;" >Henzoid</a></span> <span class="odate time_1572479525 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">30 Oct 2019 23:52</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4410541">
									

<p>So, I can see that a ton of effort went into this piece, but I'm personally not feeling it. However, aside from just generally not liking the logs, the description strikes me as odd, so per request of the author, here is my line by line of the description.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Line&nbsp;by&nbsp;line</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Close</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-4842-1 is a boombox which plays at maximum volume without the need for a power source.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Off the bat, this sentence feels like it lacks clinical tone. It's not what I would call &quot;aclinical&quot;, but the wordings could be tweaked a bit to make it feel MORE clinical, like, not using words like &quot;plays&quot;, or the somewhat colloquial use of &quot;maximum volume&quot; (is it important that we know how loud it is? How do we know it's at maximum volume? this inclusion brings up more questions than answers, and doesn't add to the piece overall.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>The only sounds that have played since its discovery and subsequent containment are field recordings of trains passing nearby the microphone.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>The clinical tone feels off on this one too, because of the phrases &quot;the only sounds&quot; and &quot;nearby the microphone&quot;, which have the same 'not quite clinical' vibe to the previous sentence.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-4842-2 is a boombox which manifests at 40°██'██.█&quot;N 74°██'██.█&quot;W once every 177 days, thereafter playing at maximum volume without the need for a power source.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Aside from the obvious disparities, this feels like it could be lumped in with the first section, like &quot;SCP-4842 refers to two boomboxes&#8230;&quot; and then describe each one. Also, I know including numbers would be useless, but visually, those redactions are really distracting. Ultimately, including the coordinates and then removing them adds nothing, and feels like something you should just omit.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>only two individuals are present on all recordings, identified as Jensen Kortland and Alix Cuthbertson.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Remove &quot;only&quot;.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Interviews with both show that neither were aware of nor recognize SCP-4842's associated phenomena, and that neither have visited █████████████, ████████, having lived on Martha's Vineyard together since April 7th, 2013.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>A few issues here. &quot;Interviews with both show that neither&quot; is awkwardly phrased. I would side in favor of removing &quot;both&quot; and saying something like &quot;Interviews with the individuals in question&quot; or something more clinical.</p>
<p>&quot;Recognize&quot; seems like a strange word to use when describing phenomena. I would reword this along the lines of &quot;Interviews with the individuals in question have revealed that neither are aware of SCP-4842 or its associated phenomena&quot;.</p>
<p>Another example of weird redactions, this time, referencing something that we haven't seen before and therefore, doesn't even work as a callback redaction since, again, it's a brand new redaction. This unknown location might as well be omitted.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>

